> I have discussed this case with Zhedong (cc'ed above), and it seems
> that
> the impact of '200' is simply to large to be able to compute the cv
> with
> 'adjusting' the joint estimate. in particular, the changes '200' have
> on
> the hyperparameters is the main driver, and if you fix the
> hyperparmeters and rerun the examples, then you're results will look
> way
> better.
>
> the current computations of the cv or group.cv <http://group.cv>, all assumes that we
> can
> correct the joint estimate to get the estimate when y[i] is removed
> (this also includes the hyperparaemters). this implicitely assumes
> that
> the posterior |y and |y[-i]  are not to far away, which is not the
> case
> in your example.
>
> Best
> Havard
